{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552119-homebrew-arcanum-data","id":1552119,"title":"Homebrew Arcanum Data","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-06T15:38:55-07:00","id":1552119,"title":"Homebrew Arcanum Data","content":"I want to add Data as a Arcanum to my campaign. It would not be a variant of space but its own thing.<br /> Possible themes include: Knowledge, understanding, abilities, psychological-social standing.<br /> What do you think about the concept and possible rotes?<br /> I have a problem in imagining possible atainments for it. Like how would mage armor look?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T16:26:41-07:00","id":1552121,"title":"","content":"I think the first step would be zeroing in on what Data is. By default it could mean the information from every Knowing Practice or hide the presence of anything via Veiling, and so on.<br /> <br /> So I think the first step is getting more detail on you vision. How would you describe the Arcanum in one phrase, with no commas or pauses ? How do you envision it being used in your chronicle? What kind of theme and symbolism do you want it to present?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T16:35:59-07:00","id":1552122,"title":"","content":"Its the realm of knowledge and social interactions.<br /> I see it used close to how demon social embeds are used. To manipulate data in writing, electronic, abilities or even social connections and value.<br /> i see it downloading abilities, changing someones standing, making magical things allowed in a area without paradox, manipulating data, even DNA (with help of life). <br /> A sort of support sphere like Prime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T18:52:01-07:00","id":1552127,"title":"","content":"I am not sure how to fit DNA there, but so far its purview seems to be: inscribing, recording, want, communication.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-06T23:09:55-07:00","id":1552128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552119-homebrew-arcanum-data?p=1552127#post1552127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure how to fit DNA there, but so far its purview seems to be: inscribing, recording, want, communication.</div> </div> </div> </div>How i imagine it things, characters features can be data: most backgrounds like resources. But there are also abstract things like connections, personality, signals someones body language may send, dna etc that may require other arcanum. Data is information not truth.<br /> <br /> I imagine mage sight as being able to see information about things and people real time. So talking to a barista i have all the info like in the sherlock holmes movies displayed about him.<br /> Not sure about mage armor thu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 07-07-2025, 02:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T00:42:51-07:00","id":1552129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552119-homebrew-arcanum-data?p=1552122#post1552122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its the realm of knowledge and social interactions.<br /> I see it used close to how demon social embeds are used. To manipulate data in writing, electronic, abilities or even social connections and value.<br /> i see it downloading abilities, changing someones standing, making magical things allowed in a area without paradox, manipulating data, even DNA (with help of life).<br /> A sort of support sphere like Prime.</div> </div> </div> </div>The obvious problem you're going to run into is that Arcana are generally not abstract and powers like Embeds are built on complex frameworks of the sort that take archmagic to create and mess with, because the Arcana are building blocks and spells meddle with concrete phenomena, even if those phenomena are esoteric things like sympathetic links.<br /> <br /> No amount of spellcasting is going to allow a mage to e.g. simply reach out and target the concept of their credit card debt without going through the vectors of who they owe or where that information is stored, at least not with any kind of fine control \u2014 Fate can be used to accomplish desired outcomes as long as you aren't fussed about the methods or consequences, but spirits form a useful resource base for mages to draw upon even without their powers being Paradox-proof.<br /> <br /> The other problem is that\u2026 well, not to put too fine a point on it, conceptually it sounds like the Arcanum is too general to be balanced; its Mage Sight gives you information with no constraints on type and its hypothetical spells either require another Arcanum to do anything or target abstract phenomena too diffuse to fit into conventional Scale factors. All Arcana are tools for understanding and manipulating the world, so what can Data do that can't be easily done by another Arcanum, given the limits of Awakened spellcasting, and what mechanical systems might you have in mind that it would introduce and/or work with, if necessary?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T01:05:55-07:00","id":1552130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552119-homebrew-arcanum-data?p=1552129#post1552129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obvious problem you're going to run into is that Arcana are generally not abstract and powers like Embeds are built on complex frameworks of the sort that take archmagic to create and mess with, because the Arcana are building blocks and spells meddle with concrete phenomena, even if those phenomena are esoteric things like sympathetic links.<br /> <br /> The other problem is that\u2026 well, not to put too fine a point on it, conceptually it sounds like the Arcanum is too general to be balanced; its Mage Sight gives you information with no constraints on type and its hypothetical spells either require another Arcanum to do anything or target abstract phenomena too diffuse to fit into conventional Scale factors. All Arcana are tools for understanding and manipulating the world, so what can Data do that can't be easily done by another Arcanum, given the limits of Awakened spellcasting, and what mechanical systems might you have in mind that it would introduce and/or work with, if necessary?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was going the way truth goes in prime but in information without truth or not.<br /> <br /> So knowing data would be a basic identification spell allowing to see everything that can be seen by an obserwer about the item/ person<br /> unveiling would be a universal translator to understand languages writen or spoken or even decode cyphers<br /> veiling would allow to encrypt the data for example writen in a book or in a program or hide someones obvious status signs<br /> shielding could for example protect from sympathetic connections and make the data trail you make during the duration untrcable<br /> fraying could delete text, code or relation<br /> perfecting could allow to increase abilities or restore corrupted data from for example a burned page<br /> weaving could affect how people see other people<br /> patterning and unraveling could allow for making and destroying relations between things and people similar to demon contracts<br /> making could make sleepers not react on obvious magical effects<br /> unmaking could delete data for example making someone forget how to use a ability<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 07-07-2025, 04:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T03:08:51-07:00","id":1552133,"title":"","content":"How about this? <br /> Lets make it affect the symbolic interpretation of things. Not as in mind control but information interpretation.<br /> Therefore it would allow to:<br /> decipher/ encrypt code and unknown languages<br /> change the meaning of symbolic elements of people and things<br /> change as those are socialy treated<br /> create new information relationships<br /> It does not alter mater nor does it affect other peoples minds. It works more like a consensus of what information is related when looking on something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T06:42:08-07:00","id":1552138,"title":"","content":"I think it keeps running into the problems <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> described.<br /> <br /> Every Arcanum has practices about information. How does Data differentiates from them, so that it can acquire information, but doesn't simply trumps every other Arcana in doing so?<br /> <br /> What can it do <i><b>in practice</b></i> that is distinct from other Arcana?<br /> <br /> Basically, to make an Arcanum you have to go through each and every Practice and think how it would work <b>in concrete use</b>. It has to fulfill four criteria:<br /> <br /> 1 - It has to clearly do something with each Practice. Not just an abstract explanation, but an actual, concrete use, with clear targets, effects and use of the basic game mechanics;<br /> <br /> 2 - It has to be complete in itself. While some effects would certainly need other Arcana, you can't be required to take any other Arcanum to be able to use this one with every Practice;<br /> <br /> 3 - It has to be distinct. As many Practices as possible should be able to do something no other Arcanum can, or at least different Practices shouldn't do things the same Arcanum does;<br /> <br /> 4 - It has to be limited. Unless you plan to overhaul the other Arcana, the new one shouldn't be clearly superior to others, preferably at no Practice whatsoever.<br /> <br /> So, for example, it has to have Knowing effects, at least one that it can use alone, but this Knowing effect shouldn't simply acquire the same information other Arcana acquire, much less be better at it than any particular Arcanum at their own purview.<br /> <br /> Finally, we should keep in mind that the purview of an Arcanum is the phenomenon it acts upon, not the effect it produces. A <b>Data</b> Arcanum shouldn't acquire information about anything, but acquire information about information itself. How does it look like? What concrete, easy to grasp examples can be given?<br /> <br /> Unless you can work at least half the Practices through this, I don't think you have a fleshed enough concept, and I'm having problems seeing this particular concept through.<br /> <br /> Data wasn't a very good idea back in Ascension. In Awakening it seems even harder to work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T07:27:09-07:00","id":1552142,"title":"","content":"Ok <br /> - Knowing: Detect and interpret social or symbolic data in the environment. Recognize someone\u2019s official status, affiliations, reputational echoes, or the social meaning of a document, crest, or inscription.<br /> Example: Be able to see things a good deductionist would see looking on a person like trauma and attitude - from their body language, resources - from their atire, ocupation from behavioral quirks and so on. <br /> <br /> - Unveiling: Be able to decrypt and understandhidden data like cyphers or unknown languages both in voice and writing<br /> Example: Decoding a ancient tablet in a forgotten language.<br /> <br /> Compeling: Be able to nudge a bit the meaning of a data structure like a document or program.<br /> Example: Changing the name on the document to be interpreted with someone else (not physicaly just in understanding)<br /> <br /> Veiling: Encrypting your messages and worlds. Hiding the meaning of the trail you left behind.<br /> Example: making so your muddy shoe tracks are interpreted as animal tracks or as simple debree.<br /> <br /> Shielding: Prevents the data a character left behind from forming sympathetic connections with him and being connected to him through association.<br /> Example: The signature he left in the hotel cannot be traced to him and is unreadable.<br /> <br /> Fraying: Damages the data making it hard to decypher.<br /> Example: Corrupts a computer file so the system registers it as unopenable.<br /> <br /> Perfecting: Restores data to its former shape. Refines the information allowing to read between the lines. Gain dots in abilities.<br /> Example restoring the information from a burned note.<br /> <br /> Weaving: Change the interpretation of the given information.<br /> Example: Appear to be rich, important, one of the factory employees.<br /> <br /> Unraveling: Distort the meening of a given information<br /> Example: Disolve the conotations of what a wanted poster means.<br /> <br /> Patterning: Allows creating new relations between data structures<br /> Example: The barista recodnises the characters watch as the markings of his hiden cult.<br /> <br /> Unmaking: Deleting information.<br /> Example: No one knows this man.<br /> <br /> Making: Creates new data.<br /> Example: Fireballs are normal in this town.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T11:10:50-07:00","id":1552150,"title":"","content":"EDIT: It deleted half of my post and then posted it, and I no longer have the time to get that down, so....detailed questioning aside, I do at least want to pull the brakes on this train and ask the question that was at the heart of this:<br /> <br /> <i>Why</i> do you want to make this Data Arcanum? what is this going to do for the games at your table?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-07-2025, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-07T11:16:55-07:00","id":1552152,"title":"","content":"Im in the process of converting my Mtas into awakening system (with keeping the world lore, avatars consensus etc. We have a homebrewed data sphere as a 10th sphere that is its own thing and i wanted to change it into a arcanum).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-17T17:58:43-08:00","id":1555578,"title":"","content":"Hi! Saw this post and, funnily enough, I have been working extensively on a custom Data Arcanum for my game \u2014 though it's quite a bit more involved for me, as I'm including with it a MtAw version of the Digital Web from Ascension. I'll probably make my own thread on it once it's ready, but if you want some ideas on the unique things I've devised for it already which could be applied even in general use cases then I'd be happy to share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28963-wulfra","name":"Wulfra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T06:58:58-08:00","id":1555595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wulfra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552119-homebrew-arcanum-data?p=1555578#post1555578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! Saw this post and, funnily enough, I have been working extensively on a custom Data Arcanum for my game \u2014 though it's quite a bit more involved for me, as I'm including with it a MtAw version of the Digital Web from Ascension. I'll probably make my own thread on it once it's ready, but if you want some ideas on the unique things I've devised for it already which could be applied even in general use cases then I'd be happy to share.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T10:34:40-08:00","id":1555596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552119-homebrew-arcanum-data?p=1552152#post1552152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Im in the process of converting my Mtas into awakening system (with keeping the world lore, avatars consensus etc</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some design questions depend on worldbuilding, whether you favour the lore, setting and characters from one or the other; the designers of Chronicles, and Awakening spent a lot of time into a coherent system, therefore it is a bad idea to try to mix and match without considering that.<br /> <br /> In the case of Awakening, the way Arcana work is based that in this setting the realm of Platonic ideas is real and that's why magic works as it does, the Arcana, Legacies, the enemies, etc. Like playing DnD using Awakening rules, you need to change lots of things beyond the magic mechanics.<br /> <br /> <br /> Without any bad faith, I tell you this is conceptually a flawed idea.<br /> <br /> If you use the mechanics as stated, then for example Consensus can not work. Avatars have no place if you use the Gnosis mechanics (daimons? you already have you own in the Oneiros), etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-18T12:11:20-08:00","id":1555598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552119-homebrew-arcanum-data?p=1555596#post1555596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some design questions depend on worldbuilding, whether you favour the lore, setting and characters from one or the other; the designers of Chronicles, and Awakening spent a lot of time into a coherent system, therefore it is a bad idea to try to mix and match without considering that.<br /> <br /> In the case of Awakening, the way Arcana work is based that in this setting the realm of Platonic ideas is real and that's why magic works as it does, the Arcana, Legacies, the enemies, etc. Like playing DnD using Awakening rules, you need to change lots of things beyond the magic mechanics.<br /> <br /> <br /> Without any bad faith, I tell you this is conceptually a flawed idea.<br /> <br /> If you use the mechanics as stated, then for example Consensus can not work. Avatars have no place if you use the Gnosis mechanics (daimons? you already have you own in the Oneiros), etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a ton of conversion hacks that did that already years ago. Ascension on Awakening mechanics is nothing new.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-05T15:22:41-08:00","id":1556203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1552119-homebrew-arcanum-data?p=1555595#post1555595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, basically, &quot;Data&quot; in my add-on as I've set it up is the Arcanum of pure information (rather than Truth as Prime is), handling parsing, searching, aggregating, and programming (as in the act of creating something rather than just computer code). It is primarily a supportive Arcanum, in that role, but can enable some very useful utilities because of it \u2014 and, of course, makes you a wiz with information, which is always useful. It also has a unique way of casting (enabled with the 2 dot attainment and certain spells) called Similarity wherein it can compare how similar the data of two subjects are and make effects from them (a large use being effectively magical DRM).<br /> <br /> Among the things data can do at each level is:<br /> <br /> Initiate: Parse any information regardless of language (can read machine code as easily as something in a human language), gather information equivalent to an extended research roll with one casting, decrypt encoded/enciphered information (which can also lower Mystery Opacity with reach), scan something's functionality (so primary directive, most utilized skill, stability, etc.)<br /> Apprentice: Protect data from being copied (using Similarity as above, stops people from copying your Rotes or spreading certain information), alter the way certain data is seen (acting as a sort of illusion or spoofing), granting an intuitive sense on a pathway towards acquiring some desired information, encrypting data, making you better at creating things<br /> Disciple: Overwhelming targets with junk data (applying die pool penalty as wounds do), making spells trigger from parsing/opening/altering data (making memetic agents similar to the Basilisk Yantra), increasing/decreasing something's ability to resist rolls or withstand directly through buffing/debuffing their data security (as opposed to modifying certain stats), monitoring the flow of data in an area to tell when veiling/stealth effects are happening (providing bonuses to clashes against them)<br /> Adept: Creating magically compressed file backups (can be combined with other Arcana to backup things like minds, creatures, spirits, even spells) and restoring them, permanently corrupting data to cause detrimental effects to targets, applying a &quot;reality filter&quot; on an area which makes things work better or worse according to a paradigm/theme you set (rather than just illusion making things look/feel different, actually rewriting meta-data)<br /> Master: Destroying a specific set of information (using Similarity to affect all copies of it), removing the ability of a subject to either send or receive information from all sources in the world (similar to Death 5's effect except it doesn't remove conditions/make it as if you died and also isn't removed when interacting with the world)<br /> <br /> There's lots of other effects but they're specifically tied to the new reality-layer I introduced (the realm which reflects information, the internet, etc.), but these are the universal effects which can fit anything. The 4th rank attainment further cements its supportive role by basically installing a magical-computer-matrix in your soul, making it easier for you to form spell imagos and giving you a place where information you gather from Data spells can be stored safely.<br /> <br /> There's also some effects which can indirectly affect Paradox, but those are also tied into my specific interpretation of the Arcana and the circumstances of its creation (and how it can fit in with the others). Basically, since Data is the Arcana of instantiated things (using object-oriented programming terms) and Prime is the Arcana of the classes (the thing-templates), it's got inherent ties to the Abyss since it's basically the junk information of existence which doesn't fit in with the Supernal. It can decrease (or increase) Paradox chances by applying this to keep the &quot;scope&quot; of data tuned to one vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28963-wulfra","name":"Wulfra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}